<title>LATVIA: Latvian trade deficit stable in Jan-Feb 1997.</title>
<headline>Latvian trade deficit stable in Jan-Feb 1997.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvia's trade deficit in the first two months of the year was 72.03 million lats in current prices compared with a deficit of 72.52 million lats in the same period last year, the statistics committee said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>All figures are millions of lats in current prices unless otherwise stated.</p>
<p> LATVIAN TRADE BALANCE   Jan-Feb '97   Jan '97   Jan-Feb '96</p>
<p> Exports		     204.33	  66.16     179.06</p>
<p> Imports		     132.30	  97.88     106.54</p>
<p> Balance		     -72.03	  -31.72    -72.52</p>
<p>Major trade partners:</p>
<p>EXPORTS (pct of total vs same period last year)</p>
<p>Russia  22.1 (27.9)</p>
<p>Germany 15.2 (14.3</p>
<p>Britain 14.4  (8.0)</p>
<p>IMPORTS</p>
<p>Russia  19.2 (22.8)</p>
<p>Germany 13.7 (12.7)</p>
<p>Finland  9.6  (9.7)</p>
<p>-- Patrick Lannin, Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
